WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
Between 2018 and 2020, the
wealthiest tenth of households

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.050
in Great Britain held 43
per cent of all wealth.

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.050
The poorest half held just 9 per cent.

4
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:18.660
Around the world, about 2.3 billion
people lived in extreme poverty in 1990.

5
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.960
By 2026, it was around 811 million.

6
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.250
So why do some families
have far more than others,

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.640
and can a government narrow the gap?

8
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.480
In this mission, you'll
see why income and wealth

9
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.290
are not the same thing.

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.370
Then you'll calculate a tax bill,

11
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.000
band by band.

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.080
Your mission: find out
where the gap comes from,

13
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.110
and what a government can do about it.
